[Antigravity Debug ANTIGRAVITY-41] Body Preview: {"project":"macro-spirit-msbh7","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-thinking","request":{"generationConfig":{"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingConfig":{"thinkingBudget":0,"includeThoughts":false}},"contents":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Let's try to come up with a plan for how to implement a resolution for this Github issue in the sst/opencode repository: \n\ngh --repo ariane-emory/opencode issue view 47;\n\nTake note of any coments on the issue, the discussion may include valuable insights on how to best resolve the issue:\n\ngh --repo ariane-emory/opencode issue view 47 --comments;\n\nIMPORTANT: Pay special attention to any comments from your user, ariane-emory, she often has good ideas!\n\nThink the changes required to resolve the issue through thoroughly and break the changes down into small steps in order to produce a detailed, step-by-step plan for resolving the issue. \n\nMake the minimal change required to solve the issue. Do not make any unnecessary changes unrelated to the changes that are required to resolve the isue.\n\nThink carefully about whether the changes necessitate re-generating either the TypeScript or Go SDKs, and if so be sure to include this step in your plan. Don't worry about the Python SDK yet, we can deal with that later on.\n\nGroup the plan's steps into \"phases\". After completing each phase, the code MUST build correctly and all tests (except the enterprise tests, you can ignore those) MUST pass. \n\nOnce you've come up with your plan, submit it to me for approval."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"functionCall":{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"gh --repo ariane-emory/opencode issue view 47","description":"View GitHub issue #47"},"id":"tool-call-1"}},{"functionCall":{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"gh --repo ariane-emory/opencode issue view 47 --comments","description":"View issue #47 comments"},"id":"tool-call-2"}}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"functionResponse":{"name":"bash","response":{"name":"bash","content":"title:  [FEATURE]: add the ability to keybind a user's custom slash commands\nstate:  OPEN\nauthor: ariane-emory\nlabels:\ncomments:       0\nassignees:\nprojects:\nmilestone:\nnumber: 47\n--\n### Feature hasn't been suggested before.\n\n- [x] I have verified this feature I'm about to request hasn't been suggested before.\n\n### Describe the enhancement you want to request\n\nIt would be useful if a user's custom slash commands (i.e., the Markdown files in their `~/.config/opencode/command` directory could be bound to keystrokes.\n\nThis could be done by interpreting any key beginning with a `/` in the object under the `\"keybinds\"` key in the config file as the name of a custom command's Markdown file. For example, this JSON snippet:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"keybinds\": {\n    \"/my-command\": \"ctrl+shift+m\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n... would cause a `ctrl+shift+m` keystroke to replace the current contents of the prompt input text box with `/my-command` and immediately submit the prompt input text box's contents, triggering the user's `/my-command` command."},"id":"tool-call-1"}},{"functionResponse":{"name":"bash","response":{"name":"bash","content":""},"id":"tool-call-2"}}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Now let me explore the codebase to understand how keybindings and custom slash commands work:"},{"functionCall":{"name":"task","args":{"description":"Explore keybinds implementation","prompt":"I need to understand how keybindings work in the opencode project. Please find:\n\n1. Where keybinds are defined/configured (look for keybind config schema, default keybinds)\n2. How keybinds are loaded and processed\n3. How keybind actions are executed/handled\n4. The keybind configuration structure in JSON\n\nFocus on the packages/opencode directory. Return the relevant file paths and a summary of the keybind system architecture.","subagent_type":"explore"},"id":"tool-call-3"}},{"functionCall":{"name":"task","args":{"description":"Explore custom slash commands","prompt":"I need to understand how custom slash commands (user-defined commands from ~/.config/opencode/command directory) work in the opencode project. Please find:\n\n1. Where custom slash commands are loaded from\n2. How they are parsed and executed\n3. How the command directory is discovered\n4. The data structure used to represent commands\n\nFocus on the packages/opencode directory. Return the relevant file paths and a summary of how custom slash commands work.","subagent_type":"explore"},"id":"tool-call-4"}}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"functionResponse":{"name":"task","response":{"name":"task","content":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the keybinding system. Let me provide you with a summary:\n\n## Keybind System Architecture Summary\n\n### Relevant File Paths\n\n1. **Keybind Schema Definition (Zod)**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts` (lines 429-566)\n\n2. **Keybind Utility Functions**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/util/keybind.ts`\n\n3. **Keybind Context Provider (React/Solid)**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/context/keybind.tsx`\n\n4. **Command Dialog (Action Execution)**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/component/dialog-command.tsx`\n\n5. **SDK Type Definitions**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts` (lines 796-1113)\n\n6. **Unit Tests**\n   - `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/test/keybind.test.ts`\n\n---\n\n### Architecture Overview\n\n#### 1. Keybind Definition & Configuration (config.ts)\n- Keybinds are defined using **Zod schemas** in `Config.Keybinds`\n- Each keybind has a string value with:\n  - An **action name** (e.g., `app_exit`, `session_new`)\n  - A **default binding** (e.g., `\"ctrl+c,ctrl+d,<leader>q\"`)\n  - A **description**\n- The `<leader>` prefix supports Vim-style leader key combinations (default: `ctrl+x`)\n- Multiple bindings per action are comma-separated (e.g., `\"ctrl+c,ctrl+d\"`)\n- Use `\"none\"` to disable a keybind\n\n#### 2. Keybind Parsing & Matching (keybind.ts)\nThe `Keybind` namespace provides:\n- **`parse(key: string): Info[]`** - Converts string keybinds to structured Info objects\n- **`match(a: Info, b: Info): boolean`** - Checks if two keybinds are equivalent\n- **`toString(info: Info): string`** - Converts Info back to display string\n- **`fromParsedKey(key: ParsedKey, leader?): Info`** - Converts OpenTUI ParsedKey to Info\n\n**Supported modifiers**: `ctrl`, `alt`/`meta`/`option`, `shift`, `super`, `<leader>`\n\n#### 3. Keybind Loading (keybind.tsx context)\n- `KeybindProvider` creates a Solid context that:\n  1. Loads keybinds from `sync.data.config.keybinds`\n  2. Parses all keybinds using `Keybind.parse()`\n  3. Manages **leader key state** with 2-second timeout\n  4. Provides `match()`, `print()`, and `parse()` methods to components\n\n#### 4. Action Execution (dialog-command.tsx)\n- `CommandProvider` registers commands with optional `keybind` property\n- Uses `useKeyboard()` hook to listen for key events\n- When a key is pressed:\n  1. Iterates through registered commands\n  2. Calls `keybind.match(option.keybind, evt)` to check for matches\n  3. Executes `option.onSelect()` if matched\n- Commands are registered via `command.register()` in components like `app.tsx`, `session/index.tsx`, `prompt/index.tsx`\n\n---\n\n### JSON Configuration Structure\n\n```json\n{\n  \"keybinds\": {\n    \"leader\": \"ctrl+x\",\n    \"app_exit\": \"ctrl+c,ctrl+d,<leader>q\",\n    \"editor_open\": \"<leader>e\",\n    \"session_new\": \"<leader>n\",\n    \"session_list\": \"<leader>l\",\n    \"model_list\": \"<leader>m\",\n    \"agent_cycle\": \"tab\",\n    \"input_submit\": \"return\",\n    \"input_newline\": \"shift+return,ctrl+return,alt+return,ctrl+j\",\n    \"messages_page_up\": \"pageup\",\n    \"messages_page_down\": \"pagedown\",\n    \"input_undo\": \"ctrl+-,super+z\",\n    \"input_redo\": \"ctrl+.,super+shift+z\",\n    \"scrollbar_toggle\": \"none\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Key format options**:\n- Simple keys: `\"f\"`, `\"return\"`, `\"escape\"`, `\"f2\"`, `\"pageup\"`\n- Modifier combinations: `\"ctrl+x\"`, `\"alt+g\"`, `\"shift+return\"`, `\"super+z\"`\n- Leader prefix: `\"<leader>n\"`, `\"<leader>right\"`\n- Multiple bindings: `\"ctrl+c,ctrl+d,<leader>q\"`\n- Disabled: `\"none\"`\n\n<task_metadata>\nsession_id: ses_4d3e726b4ffeiBNbJp1NVrJ8OE\n</task_metadata>"},"id":"tool-call-3"}},{"functionResponse":{"name":"task","response":{"name":"task","content":"Now I have all the information needed to provide a comprehensive answer.\n\n---\n\n## Summary: Custom Slash Commands in OpenCode\n\n### Relevant File Paths\n\n1. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts`** - Command loading and directory discovery\n2. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/command/index.ts`** - Command data structure and state management\n3. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/markdown.ts`** - Markdown parsing (frontmatter + content)\n4. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts`** - Command execution logic (lines 1281-1367)\n5. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/global/index.ts`** - Global paths including config directory\n6. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/server/server.ts`** - Server endpoint for listing commands (line 1438-1458)\n7. **`/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/component/prompt/index.tsx`** - TUI command invocation (lines 513-528)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where Custom Slash Commands Are Loaded From\n\nCommands are loaded from multiple directories via the `loadCommand()` function in `config.ts` (line 188-224). The directories searched are:\n\n- **Global config**: `~/.config/opencode/command/` (via `Global.Path.config`)\n- **Project-level**: `.opencode/command/` directories found via `Filesystem.up()` from the instance directory up to the worktree\n- **Home directory**: `~/.opencode/command/`\n- **Custom directory**: `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` environment variable if set\n\nThe glob pattern used is: `command/**/*.md`\n\n### 2. How Commands Are Parsed and Executed\n\n**Parsing (config.ts lines 188-224):**\n1. The `COMMAND_GLOB` pattern (`command/**/*.md`) scans the directories\n2. Each `.md` file is parsed using `ConfigMarkdown.parse()` which uses the `gray-matter` library\n3. Frontmatter YAML becomes command metadata; markdown body becomes the `template`\n4. Command name is derived from the file path (e.g., `command/foo/bar.md` becomes `foo/bar`)\n5. The parsed config is validated against the `Command` Zod schema\n\n**Execution (session/prompt.ts lines 1281-1367):**\n1. Command is retrieved via `Command.get(name)`\n2. Arguments are parsed using a regex pattern that handles quoted strings\n3. Placeholders (`$1`, `$2`, etc.) in the template are replaced with arguments\n4. `$ARGUMENTS` is replaced with the full argument string\n5. Shell expressions (`` !`command` ``) are executed and their output substituted\n6. The template is sent to the LLM via the specified (or default) agent\n\n### 3. How the Command Directory Is Discovered\n\nFrom `global/index.ts` (lines 8-22):\n```typescript\nconst config = path.join(xdgConfig!, app)  // ~/.config/opencode on Linux/macOS\n```\n\nFrom `config.ts` (lines 70-91), directories are collected from:\n1. `Global.Path.config` - XDG config directory (`~/.config/opencode/`)\n2. `.opencode` directories via `Filesystem.up()` from project to worktree\n3. `.opencode` in home directory\n4. `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` environment variable\n\n### 4. Data Structure for Commands\n\n**Zod Schema (config.ts lines 383-390):**\n```typescript\nexport const Command = z.object({\n  template: z.string(),           // The markdown body - the prompt template\n  description: z.string().optional(), // Command description (from frontmatter)\n  agent: z.string().optional(),   // Agent to use (from frontmatter)\n  model: z.string().option... (truncated 276698 chars)
