[Antigravity Debug ANTIGRAVITY-127] Body Preview: {"project":"macro-spirit-msbh7","model":"claude-opus-4-5-thinking","request":{"generationConfig":{"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingConfig":{"thinkingBudget":0,"includeThoughts":false}},"contents":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Currently, binding a nonexistent key command to a key in the configuration file is a fatal error, opencode won't even start... for example if I have this in my configuration file, opencode will fail to start up:\n\n\"keybinds\": {\n  \"fake_key_command\": \"ctrl+f\",\n}\n\nThis is not ideal: this should be a non-fatal error instead. We should allow the program to start even if non-existing key commands are bound, and when these keys are struck they should display a toast informing the user that the command does not exist (something like \"No command 'fake_key_command'\").\n\nThink the change through thoroughly and break the change down into small steps to produce a detailed, step-by-step plan for implementing the change. Group the plan's steps into \"phases\". The code MUST build correctly and all tests MUST pass after each phase. "}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"I'll explore the codebase to understand how keybinds are currently handled, then create a detailed plan."},{"functionCall":{"name":"task","args":{"prompt":"Explore the opencode codebase (in packages/opencode) to understand how keybinds are configured, validated, and processed. I need to understand:\n\n1. Where keybinds are defined in the configuration schema\n2. Where keybind validation happens (and causes fatal errors for nonexistent commands)\n3. Where keybinds are processed when keys are pressed\n4. How the toast/notification system works\n\nSearch for:\n- Keybind configuration parsing\n- Keybind command validation\n- Key event handling\n- Toast/notification display\n\nReturn file paths with relevant line numbers and a summary of the keybind flow.","subagent_type":"explore","description":"Explore keybind handling code"},"id":"tool-call-1"}}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"functionResponse":{"name":"task","response":{"name":"task","content":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile my findings into a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Keybind Configuration, Validation, and Processing Flow\n\n### 1. Keybind Configuration Schema Definition\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts`\n**Lines:** 429-566\n\nThe keybinds are defined in a Zod schema called `Config.Keybinds`:\n\n- **Lines 429-562**: Defines all available keybind options with their defaults:\n  - `leader` - Leader key (default: `\"ctrl+x\"`)\n  - `app_exit` - Exit application (default: `\"ctrl+c,ctrl+d,<leader>q\"`)\n  - `session_*` - Session-related keybinds\n  - `messages_*` - Message navigation keybinds\n  - `input_*` - Input field keybinds\n  - `model_*` - Model switching keybinds\n  - `agent_*` - Agent switching keybinds\n  - And many more...\n\n- **Line 563**: `.strict()` - This causes **fatal errors** if users add unknown keybind names to their config\n\n- **Lines 623-627**: The keybinds are included in the main `Config.Info` schema as an optional field\n\n---\n\n### 2. Keybind Validation (Fatal Errors for Nonexistent Commands)\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts`\n**Lines:** 916-937\n\nWhen config is loaded:\n- **Line 916**: `Info.safeParse(data)` validates the config including keybinds\n- **Lines 934-937**: If validation fails, throws `InvalidError` with details\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/error.ts`\n**Lines:** 33-37\n\nError formatting for invalid config:\n```typescript\nif (Config.InvalidError.isInstance(input))\n  return [\n    `Config file at ${input.data.path} is invalid`,\n    ...(input.data.issues?.map((issue) => \"↳ \" + issue.message + \" \" + issue.path.join(\".\")) ?? []),\n  ].join(\"\\n\")\n```\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/index.ts`\n**Lines:** 113-151\n\nFatal error handling at startup:\n- Catches errors from config parsing\n- Displays formatted error via `FormatError(e)` or logs to file\n- Sets `process.exitCode = 1`\n\nThe `.strict()` on line 563 means that if a user adds a keybind like `my_custom_command: \"ctrl+m\"` to their config, it will fail validation because `my_custom_command` is not a recognized keybind name.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Keybind Processing When Keys Are Pressed\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/util/keybind.ts`\n**Lines:** 1-103\n\nCore keybind utilities:\n- **Lines 56-101**: `Keybind.parse(key: string)` - Parses keybind strings like `\"ctrl+x\"` or `\"<leader>f\"` into `Keybind.Info` objects\n- **Lines 13-18**: `Keybind.match(a, b)` - Compares two keybind infos for equality\n- **Lines 35-54**: `Keybind.toString(info)` - Converts keybind info back to display string\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/context/keybind.tsx`\n**Lines:** 1-102\n\nKeybind context provider:\n- **Lines 15-20**: Creates memoized keybind configs from user config, parsing each with `Keybind.parse()`\n- **Lines 52-66**: `useKeyboard()` hook listens for leader key activation\n- **Lines 82-90**: `match(key, evt)` method matches a keyboard event against a keybind config name\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/component/dialog-command.tsx`\n**Lines:** 46-55\n\nGlobal command keybind handler:\n```typescript\nuseKeyboard((evt) => {\n  for (const option of options()) {\n    if (option.keybind && keybind.match(option.keybind, evt)) {\n      evt.preventDefault()\n      option.onSelect?.(dialog)\n      return\n    }\n  }\n})\n```\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/component/prompt/index.tsx`\n**Lines:** 729-789\n\nInput-specific key handling:\n- **Lines 734-743**: `keybind.match(\"input_clear\", e)` - Clear input\n- **Lines 744-751**: `keybind.match(\"app_exit\", e)` - Exit app\n- **Lines 767-788**: History navigation keybinds\n\n---\n\n### 4. Toast/Notification System\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/event.ts`\n**Lines:** 31-39\n\nToast event definition:\n```typescript\nToastShow: BusEvent.define(\n  \"tui.toast.show\",\n  z.object({\n    title: z.string().optional(),\n    message: z.string(),\n    variant: z.enum([\"info\", \"success\", \"warning\", \"error\"]),\n    duration: z.number().default(5000).optional(),\n  }),\n)\n```\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/ui/toast.tsx`\n**Lines:** 1-101\n\nToast implementation:\n- **Lines 12-47**: `Toast` component - Renders toast UI with variant-based border color\n- **Lines 50-82**: `init()` function - Creates toast state and `show()` method\n- **Lines 57-66**: `show(options)` - Displays toast and auto-hides after duration\n- **Lines 67-76**: `error(err)` - Convenience method for error toasts\n- **Lines 89-91**: `ToastProvider` - Context provider for toast system\n- **Lines 94-99**: `useToast()` - Hook to access toast in components\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/app.tsx`\n**Lines:** 476-482\n\nEvent-driven toast:\n```typescript\nevent.on(TuiEvent.ToastShow.type, (evt) => {\n  toast.show({\n    title: evt.properties.title,\n    message: evt.properties.message,\n    variant: evt.properties.variant,\n    duration: evt.properties.duration,\n  })\n})\n```\n\n**File:** `/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/server/server.ts`\n**Lines:** 2356-2374\n\nHTTP API endpoint for showing toasts:\n- `POST /tui/show-toast` - External programs can trigger toasts via the server API\n\n---\n\n### Key Files Summary\n\n| Purpose                          | File Path                                    | Key Lines |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| Keybind schema definition        | `src/config/config.ts`                         | 429-566   |\n| Keybind parsing/matching utility | `src/util/keybind.ts`                          | 1-103     |\n| Keybind context provider         | `src/cli/cmd/tui/context/keybind.tsx`          | 1-102     |\n| Command keybind registration     | `src/cli/cmd/tui/component/dialog-command.tsx` | 24-85     |\n| Input keybind handling           | `src/cli/cmd/tui/component/prompt/index.tsx`   | 729-789   |\n| Config validation error handling | `src/cli/error.ts`                             | 33-37     |\n| Toast event definition           | `src/cli/cmd/tui/event.ts`                     | 31-39     |\n| Toast UI component               | `src/cli/cmd/tui/ui/toast.tsx`                 | 1-101     |\n| App-level keybind commands       | `src/cli/cmd/tui/app.tsx`                      | 252-456   |\n| Keybind unit tests               | `test/keybind.test.ts`                         | 1-422     |\n\n<task_metadata>\nsession_id: ses_4ce52c825ffeKKWOmkR2iQy28p\n</task_metadata>"},"id":"tool-call-1"}}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Let me read the key files to understand the implementation details:"},{"functionCall":{"name":"read","args":{"limit":160,"filePath":"/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts","offset":420},"id":"tool-call-2"}},{"functionCall":{"name":"read","args":{"filePath":"/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/context/keybind.tsx"},"id":"tool-call-3"}},{"functionCall":{"name":"read","args":{"filePath":"/Volumes/K/Code/go/opencode/packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/ui/toast.tsx"},"id":"tool-call-4"}}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"functionResponse":{"name":"read","response":{"name":"read","content":"<file>\n00421|         .optional(),\n00422|     })\n00423|     .catchall(z.any())\n00424|     .meta({\n00425|       ref: \"AgentConfig\",\n00426|     })\n00427|   export type Agent = z.infer<typeof Agent>\n00428| \n00429|   export const Keybinds = z\n00430|     .object({\n00431|       leader: z.string